ies":"American (Traditional), Bars, Food, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":5},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Food, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Coffee & Tea, Food","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1}],"text":[{"business_id":"7GmQ9LYOoHuvsiaIJuLykQ","review_id":"BEf09idZSM_CYTjURoV9Bw","date":"2018-05-12T18:52:08","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9239110946655273,"text_excerpt":"This place. I've been a long time devotee of St Lawrence--St Cecilia's brother restaurant farther up the road towards Canal--but I just got around to trying this place today for brunch and it was incredible. There were only two servers for the mid-size space, but their hustle and smile ensured everyone was taken care of in a timely manner. The drinks and coffee were excellent...but the food...outstanding. We got the crawfish spring rolls for an appetizer. Delicious. Then I got The chicken and waffles...transcendent. Easily one of the best brunches I've had in a low key environment. Will be returning."},{"business_id":"7GmQ9LYOoHuvsiaIJuLykQ","review_id":"0QQ-3YSb27IqMow47jTUnQ","date":"2019-03-28T16:29:38","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9190820455551147,"text_excerpt":"As far as New Orleans fare goes, St Cecilia is top. Came here on a Thursday morning and was greeted with the best Bloody Mary--I'm convinced after have tried several here--in the city. Loved our waitress. She was super friendly and a superb bartender. I ordered the shrimp and grits and it came with a lovely cream sauce. Reflecting on the meal, I am left wondering whether I should have ordered a biscuit instead of the bread it comes with to add another level to the dish. My boyfriend got the regular breakfast with eggs and hash browns and it was great. His drink was also well-crafted; however, I would recommend the Bloody Mary over any of the other drinks. St Cecilia is in my top 2 places ..."},{"business_id":"7GmQ9LYOoHuvsiaIJuLykQ","review_id":"cYu2E5avVrpz2kDQNGFL2Q","date":"2017-05-01T02:20:08","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9169976711273193,"text_excerpt":"We stumbled upon this gem. The service was excellent! We were greeted by the host and immediately sat at a table in the back. The server came over quickly to take our drink order. We ordered the sweet potato fries. They were topped off with Gorgonzola cheese and pecans. So delicious! The fries were fried perfectly. Very crispy. I had the red beans and rice as my entree. It came with andouille sausage, a side of cabbage and cornbread. The beans were spicy. I enjoyed them! The cabbage was yummy. I felt that the cornbread, although tasty, should have been baked a little longer. I got to also try the Oyster banh mi. The bread was fresh. The vegetables on the sandwich were tasty. I loved the a..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"7GmQ9LYOoHuvsiaIJuLykQ","photo_id":"irIvl2CVdSx-PX9eM6n80Q","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/irIvl2CVdSx-PX9eM6n80Q.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9242819547653198},{"business_id":"7GmQ9LYOoHuvsiaIJuLykQ","photo_id":"3EHk8AEaHE3adVN53XCuXw","labe